   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: I have received the enclosed <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">cutting</seg> about <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">the trial</seg>. The offense is less grotesque than the defence!</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>        	With kind regards</salute>
                        <signed>                    	<name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed> </closer>
                </div>
            </div> <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">“Improper Novel Costs Woman $50,” <name type="work">New York Times</name> (22 February 1921): 6.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">In February 1921, the editors of <name type="work">The Little Review</name>, <name type="person" key="ande86">Margaret Anderson</name> and <name type="person" key="heap83">Jane Heap</name>, were tried for obscenity for publishing the “Nausicaa” episode in their journal’s April 1920 issue. For fuller accounts of “Nausicaa” and the prosecution and trial it occasioned, see <rs type="letter" key="L_68553">JJ to Pound, 24 October 1919</rs>, notes;<rs type="letter" key="L_68685"> 5 November 1920</rs>, notes; and <rs type="letter" key="L_68690">16 November 1920</rs>, notes.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
